  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the clear best (0.653 acc), while image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208 acc). This raises a critical uncertainty: is the weak image performance due to the resnet50 encoder being inadequate, or is the image modality fundamentally uninformative for this task? This question gates whether any of the 30+ multimodal configurations are worth testing. config_013 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_010 (same setup but resnet50), isolating the effect of image encoder quality. If ViT-L is also weak, we can confidently allocate remaining budget to RNA-only refinements and skip all multimodal configs. If ViT-L substantially improves, it validates pursuing multimodal fusion with ViT-L. This is the highest-information single experiment because it resolves a binary design decision (pursue multimodal or not) that would otherwise require multiple multimodal trials to infer indirectly."
}

